---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Crumbs from '../components/Crumbs.astro';
import Email from '../components/Email.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/data';
import { webPageLd } from '../lib/ld';
import { AMAZON_DISCLOSURE } from '../config/affiliate';

const desc = "SawChainSize.com participates in the Amazon Associates Program: links to Amazon are affiliate links, and the site earns from qualifying purchases at no extra cost to you. No other affiliate programs are used.";
const jsonld = [webPageLd("Affiliate Disclosure", "/affiliate-disclosure/", desc, SITE.dataDate, "WebPage")];
---
<Base title={"Affiliate Disclosure"} description={desc} path="/affiliate-disclosure/" nav="about" crumbs={[{ name: 'Affiliate disclosure', path: '/affiliate-disclosure/' }]} jsonld={jsonld} modified={SITE.dataDate}>
  <div class="wrap">
  <div class="pagehead"><Crumbs crumbs={[{ name: 'Affiliate disclosure', path: '/affiliate-disclosure/' }]} /><h1>Affiliate disclosure</h1></div>
  <div class="prose">
    <p><strong>The short version:</strong> {AMAZON_DISCLOSURE} SawChainSize.com is a participant in the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program, an affiliate advertising program designed to provide a means for sites to earn advertising fees by advertising and linking to Amazon.com. When you click an Amazon link on this site and buy, we may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.</p>
    <h3>Current status</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Amazon Associates only.</strong> Amazon is the only affiliate program this site participates in. Links to Amazon are tagged with this site's Associates tracking ID, are marked as sponsored links in the page code, open in a new tab, and sit next to the sentence “{AMAZON_DISCLOSURE}”</li>
      <li><strong>Other links are plain.</strong> Links to Oregon Products and other manufacturer or reference sites are untagged and earn nothing. No other retailer or manufacturer affiliate program is used, and no retailer or manufacturer has paid for placement, a review, or a mention.</li>
      <li><strong>Two kinds of Amazon link.</strong> Where we have opened the Amazon product page and confirmed the product title matches the spec, a link goes to that product page (labelled “Amazon product page”). Otherwise a link runs an Amazon search built from the pitch, gauge and drive-link numbers (labelled “Amazon search”); you choose the listing. Either way, check the listing against your bar stamp before buying.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>What this does and does not influence</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>It does <strong>not</strong> influence any specification on this site. Specs come from manufacturer manuals, fit-up charts and chain-maker data, per our <a href="/how-we-verify/">verification policy</a>. Where sources conflict, we say so and do not link a spec-matched chain.</li>
      <li>It does <strong>not</strong> change the price you pay.</li>
      <li>Amazon links are added after a spec is settled, only for items that match the spec or purpose on the page. Listings are Amazon's: we do not control sellers, stock or fit claims.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Cookies and tracking</h3>
    <p>This site itself sets no tracking or advertising cookies; its only cookie is a functional one that remembers you dismissed the cookie notice. When you click through to Amazon, Amazon may set its own cookies, which is how it credits a purchase to this site. Amazon's own policies then apply — see our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
    <h3>Prices and availability</h3>
    <p>This site shows no prices. Price and availability on Amazon change and are the ones shown at Amazon's checkout. Product names, chain designations and trademarks belong to their owners — see the footer notice.</p>
    <p class="small muted">This disclosure is provided in line with the US Federal Trade Commission's guidelines on endorsements and affiliate marketing (16 CFR Part 255) and Canada's Competition Act requirements on disclosure of material connections. Last updated: 25 October 2026.</p>
  </div>

  </div>
</Base>
